For a newborn, the federal law on statutory health insurance provides Familienversicherung (free family cover for dependants). Under SGB V §10, the children of members of a statutory health insurance fund are insured ("Versichert sind ... die Kinder von Mitgliedern"), children up to their 18th birthday ("bis zur Vollendung des achtzehnten Lebensjahres"), if the child:
1. has their residence or habitual abode in Germany;
2. is not insured in their own right under § 5 (1) nos. 1 to 8, 11 to 12, and is not voluntarily insured;
3. is not exempt from insurance and has not been released from compulsory insurance;
4. is not mainly self-employed; and
5. has no total income regularly above one seventh of the monthly reference value under § 18 of Book IV.

There is one exclusion that depends on the parents. Children are not covered if the parent who is related to them is married to, or the registered partner of, the member, is not a member of a statutory health insurance fund themselves, has a total income regularly above one twelfth of the annual earnings ceiling ("ein Zwölftel der Jahresarbeitsentgeltgrenze"), and that income is regularly higher than the member's (§10 (3)). The excerpts do not say what applies instead in that case.

If the conditions are met through more than one parent, the member chooses the fund (§10 (5)). The member must report the child to the responsible fund with the details needed to carry out the cover, and any later changes to those details ("an die zuständige Krankenkasse zu melden", §10 (6)). The national association of health insurance funds sets a uniform procedure and uniform forms for this report.

The birth certificate is needed for registering with the health insurance fund. The birth must be registered within 1 week at the registry office responsible for the place of birth, and that office issues the birth certificate.

Whether your child is covered is decided by your statutory health insurance fund, not by this service. Contact the fund of the parent who is a member.
